### Cell 8 — Study the effect of different decision thresholds (additional)

This reproduces the threshold comparison shown on page 6 of your practical document.

```python
import numpy as np

threshold_list = [0.01, 0.10, 0.3659, 0.50, 0.90, 0.99]

print("Threshold  TN  FP  FN  TP  Accuracy")

for threshold in threshold_list:

    y_threshold = (y_prob >= threshold).astype(int)

    tn, fp, fn, tp = confusion_matrix(
        y_test,
        y_threshold,
        labels=[0, 1]
    ).ravel()

    accuracy = (tp + tn) / (tp + tn + fp + fn)

    print(
        f"{threshold:<10} {tn:<3} {fp:<3} "
        f"{fn:<3} {tp:<3} {accuracy:.3f}"
    )
```

